<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf8">
<pre class="metadata">
title: Iterator Transfer
stage: 0
contributors: James M Snell
</pre>

<emu-clause id="sec-iterator.prototype.transfer" type="built-in function">
  <h1>Iterator.prototype.transfer ( )</h1>
  <p>This method moves the iteration state of a built-in synchronous iterator into a newly created iterator object with the same [[Prototype]] and closes the original iterator without running cleanup.</p>
  <p>It performs the following steps when called:</p>
  <emu-alg>
    1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
    1. If _O_ is not an Object, throw a *TypeError* exception.
    1. If _O_ has a [[GeneratorState]] internal slot, then
      1. Let _state_ be _O_.[[GeneratorState]].
      1. If _state_ is ~executing~, throw a *TypeError* exception.
      1. Let _proto_ be ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
      1. If _O_ has an [[UnderlyingIterators]] internal slot, then
        1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[GeneratorState]], [[GeneratorContext]], [[GeneratorBrand]], [[UnderlyingIterators]] »).
        1. Set _transferred_.[[UnderlyingIterators]] to _O_.[[UnderlyingIterators]].
        1. Set _O_.[[UnderlyingIterators]] to a new empty List.
      1. Else,
        1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[GeneratorState]], [[GeneratorContext]], [[GeneratorBrand]] »).
      1. Set _transferred_.[[GeneratorBrand]] to _O_.[[GeneratorBrand]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[GeneratorState]] to _state_.
      1. Let _genContext_ be _O_.[[GeneratorContext]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[GeneratorContext]] to _genContext_.
      1. If _state_ is either ~suspended-start~ or ~suspended-yield~, then
        1. Set the Generator component of _genContext_ to _transferred_.
      1. Set _O_.[[GeneratorState]] to ~completed~.
      1. Return _transferred_.
    1. If _O_ has an [[IteratedArrayLike]] internal slot, then
      1. Let _proto_ be ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
      1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[IteratedArrayLike]], [[ArrayLikeNextIndex]], [[ArrayLikeIterationKind]] »).
      1. Set _transferred_.[[IteratedArrayLike]] to _O_.[[IteratedArrayLike]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[ArrayLikeNextIndex]] to _O_.[[ArrayLikeNextIndex]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[ArrayLikeIterationKind]] to _O_.[[ArrayLikeIterationKind]].
      1. Set _O_.[[IteratedArrayLike]] to *undefined*.
      1. Return _transferred_.
    1. If _O_ has an [[IteratingRegExp]] internal slot, then
      1. Let _proto_ be ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
      1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[IteratingRegExp]], [[IteratedString]], [[Global]], [[Unicode]], [[Done]] »).
      1. Set _transferred_.[[IteratingRegExp]] to _O_.[[IteratingRegExp]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[IteratedString]] to _O_.[[IteratedString]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[Global]] to _O_.[[Global]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[Unicode]] to _O_.[[Unicode]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[Done]] to _O_.[[Done]].
      1. Set _O_.[[Done]] to *true*.
      1. Return _transferred_.
    1. If _O_ has an [[Iterated]] internal slot, then
      1. Let _proto_ be ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
      1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[Iterated]] »).
      1. Set _transferred_.[[Iterated]] to _O_.[[Iterated]].
      1. Let _closedSteps_ be a new Abstract Closure with no parameters that captures nothing and performs the following steps when called:
        1. Return CreateIteratorResultObject(*undefined*, *true*).
      1. Let _closedNext_ be CreateBuiltinFunction(_closedSteps_, 0, *""*, « »).
      1. Let _closedIter_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(*null*).
      1. Set _O_.[[Iterated]] to the Iterator Record { [[Iterator]]: _closedIter_, [[NextMethod]]: _closedNext_, [[Done]]: *true* }.
      1. Return _transferred_.
    1. Throw a *TypeError* exception.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>

<emu-clause id="sec-%asynciteratorprototype%.transfer" type="built-in function">
  <h1>%AsyncIteratorPrototype%.transfer ( )</h1>
  <p>This method moves the iteration state of a built-in asynchronous iterator into a newly created async iterator object with the same [[Prototype]] and closes the original async iterator without running cleanup.</p>
  <p>It performs the following steps when called:</p>
  <emu-alg>
    1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
    1. If _O_ is not an Object, throw a *TypeError* exception.
    1. If _O_ has an [[AsyncGeneratorState]] internal slot, then
      1. Let _state_ be _O_.[[AsyncGeneratorState]].
      1. If _state_ is ~executing~ or _state_ is ~draining-queue~, throw a *TypeError* exception.
      1. If _O_.[[AsyncGeneratorQueue]] is not empty, throw a *TypeError* exception.
      1. Let _proto_ be ? _O_.[[GetPrototypeOf]]().
      1. Let _transferred_ be OrdinaryObjectCreate(_proto_, « [[AsyncGeneratorState]], [[AsyncGeneratorContext]], [[AsyncGeneratorQueue]], [[GeneratorBrand]] »).
      1. Set _transferred_.[[GeneratorBrand]] to _O_.[[GeneratorBrand]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[AsyncGeneratorState]] to _state_.
      1. Let _genContext_ be _O_.[[AsyncGeneratorContext]].
      1. Set _transferred_.[[AsyncGeneratorContext]] to _genContext_.
      1. Set _transferred_.[[AsyncGeneratorQueue]] to a new empty List.
      1. If _state_ is either ~suspended-start~ or ~suspended-yield~, then
        1. Set the Generator component of _genContext_ to _transferred_.
      1. Set _O_.[[AsyncGeneratorState]] to ~completed~.
      1. Return _transferred_.
    1. Throw a *TypeError* exception.
  </emu-alg>
</emu-clause>
